27 #edb/ref 1031 "Creating Rows or Columns Containing Zeros Using Gaussian Elimination" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1033 3029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1034 0.2853007808149399 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050527 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "508ac00e-0867-53e8-a192-d981ff4bbdc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165051 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2390925b-1353-541e-941f-543ca9985649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166589 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166589 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t),$ given by\n\n$$\np_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad\n\tp_2(t)=-t+t^2.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are ![](images/9e/9eca81c24ee88a63d1c5468160a118cb1e987793d5fdc8d2d7eaa317fadeda93.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4dac81da-f15c-55ff-9630-7349a3e03e57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166589 #edb/ref 1074 "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](images/8c/8c3fce8e9d7cc170ad66706e783c4a46ba0530c119b8b824a66d9b5850e62760.svg)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =4\\cdot (3+2t)+(-3)\\cdot (-t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12+8t+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =12+11t-3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166590 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166590 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following matrices:\n![](images/b9/b9a1cb7eb2a3bcbadd73a68f9e73914e124a2359b8f8fc1ccc33ca950e714f88.svg)\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ B_1, B_2 \\},$ calculate ![](images/9b/9b978860f45e9e62e0315727c8eafac13360f29a7762480103b087ed6babf376.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166590 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aac4b559-b26b-57b0-8701-b3235969cd2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166590 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/88/88ea80808ca87358b78cf322c8ddd81ad7f95ddc02526361aace1ca9b914d486.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=18 \\\\ -{x}_{2} &=-9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-9 & =-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, ![](images/c5/c57b6f1ce1762add9b5b5d3e15a6363f009482b12b12366434c090d6a7478c6b.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186166591 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166591 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\np_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad\np_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad\nq(t)=5-3t+3t^2.\n$$\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\},$ find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166591 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0fc412f-8276-5876-a509-4f2173396e72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166591 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(5+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(3t-2{t}^{2}) & =5-3t+3{t}^{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =5-3t+3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/27/271f2b051a53f7aeae9a20ef23b97c9c903a7815f228dfa3ee23e2207bd24ee9.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1.$ Therefore, ![](images/1f/1fc60fff97ff92bd1cc515e6c984fbacb435dcf0fae24e751842eb8daf3390e8.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186243938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186243939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186243941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186483390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186559815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186559880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166751 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166752 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186243946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175